    <section id="architecture" class="page-section">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-tag">System Stack</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Modular Hardware Architecture</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">A highly robust, multi-tiered framework designed for failsafe operational security, modular component swaps, and high-performance robotic computing.</p>
      </div>
                    <h3>Perception & Sensor Layer</h3>
              <p>Active LiDAR telemetry, stereo computer vision, and sonar array networks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-layer layer-middle" data-layer="compute">
            <div class="layer-num">02</div>
            <svg class="layer-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="6.01" y2="6"/><line x1="6" y1="18" x2="6.01" y2="18"/></svg>
            <div class="layer-info">
              <h3>Compute & Decision Engine</h3>
              <p>On-board neural processors running localization algorithms, A* pathfinders, and safety matrices.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-layer layer-bottom" data-layer="actuation">
            <div class="layer-num">03</div>
            <svg class="layer-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 0 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 0 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33H9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 0 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg>
            <div class="layer-info">
              <h3>Actuation & Chassis Layer</h3>
              <p>Brushless hub motors, smart battery management system, and lockable cargo hatch.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
                    <div class="hotspot spot-sonar" data-sensor="sonar"><span>3</span></div>
            <div class="hotspot spot-imu" data-sensor="imu"><span>4</span></div>
            <div class="hotspot spot-drivetrain" data-sensor="drivetrain"><span>5</span></div>
            <div class="hotspot spot-battery" data-sensor="battery"><span>6</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Sensor Specifications and Live Widget -->
        <div class="sensor-info-panel">
          <div class="glass-card">
            <h3 id="sensor-name">Solid-State LiDAR</h3>
            <p id="sensor-description">Generates high-density 3D point clouds mapping the robot's surrounding environment up to 100 meters, operating reliably in direct sunlight or heavy shadow.</p>
            
            <div class="sensor-specs">
              <div class="spec-box">
                <div class="spec-title">Interface Type</div>
                <div class="spec-value" id="sensor-interface">Ethernet / ROS2</div>
              </div>
              <div class="spec-box">
                <div class="spec-title">Power Consumption</div>
                <div class="spec-value" id="sensor-power">14W (Average)</div>
              </div>
              <div class="spec-box">
                <div class="spec-title">FOV / Range</div>
                <div class="spec-value" id="sensor-fov">360° × 45° / 120m</div>
              </div>
              <div class="spec-box">
                <div class="spec-title">Update Frequency</div>
                <div class="spec-value" id="sensor-frequency">20 Hz</div>
              </div>
            </div>
              <h3>1. Task Allocation & Loading <span>Step 1</span></h3>
              <p>Robot calculates delivery sequence at Distribution Hub, evaluating payload coordinates and verifying battery safety margins.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-step" data-step="1">
            <div class="step-indicator"></div>
            <div class="step-content">
              <h3>2. Global Path Planning <span>Step 2</span></h3>
              <p>The A* algorithm maps the shortest navigation grid route from the Hub (blue node) to the destination coordinates (green node).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-step" data-step="2">
            <div class="step-indicator"></div>
            <div class="step-content">
              <h3>3. Transit & Local Avoidance <span>Step 3</span></h3>
              <p>Robot advances along grid roads. Upon encountering static/dynamic roadblocks, it halts and re-plots routes on the fly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-step" data-step="3">
            <div class="step-indicator"></div>
            <div class="step-content">
              <h3>4. Verification & Drop-off <span>Step 4</span></h3>
              <p>Upon arriving at target address, customer is notified. Compartment door unlocks after successful digital authentication.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-step" data-step="4">
            <div class="step-indicator"></div>
            <div class="step-content">
              <h3>5. Safe Return to Base <span>Step 5</span></h3>
              <p>With task completed, the robot maps its route back to the recharging bay to replenish cells for next dispatch.</p>
